<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51333" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Volumnĭus</span></b> , i,
		m.; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Volumnĭa</span></b> ,
			ae, f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the name of a Roman</i> gens.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> P. Volumnius, <i>a Roman consul</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 3,
			10</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			L. Volumnius, <i>a consul</i>, <i>who
				conquered the Samnites</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 9,
			42</span></i>; <i><span class="en">10, 18</span></i>
			sq.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Volumnia. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>The wife of Coriolanus</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 2,
			40</span></i>. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>A freed-woman</i>, <i>mistress of M.
				Antonius</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Phil. 2, 24</span></i>; otherwise called
			Cytheris, v. Cytheris.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Volumnĭā-nus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>named from Volumnius</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exercitus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					19, 12</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
